Falsifies `file_allocation_table::long_name::verification::every_long_name_run_is_well_formed`.

The defect: the units after the terminator are written as `0x0000` instead of `0xFFFF`. The name
reads back right in a lenient driver, which stops at the first zero, and is a malformed run to one
that checks the padding the specification requires.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(unit, expected)`.

diff --git a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/long_name.rs b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/long_name.rs
index 0bc37e010..d5188ac14 100644
--- a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/long_name.rs
+++ b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/long_name.rs
@@ -168,7 +168,7 @@ impl LongName {
         } else if position == self.len {
             0x0000
         } else {
-            0xFFFF
+            0x0000
         }
     }
 }
